  "body": "Part of #1152 (and #543). Found while working #1152.\n\n**What happens:** the size law (`sinker_undersize::judge`) judges a body electrode on the X and Y extents of its outline. An inward offset moves a sharp corner that is not square to the axes further than the undersize. For such a cavity (a diamond, a rotated rectangle) the extents that the spark gap reaches are short of the cavity's extents. A finish pass is then refused: \"sinker finish leaves the cavity under size\". A rough pass and a single pass are generated.\n\nThe refusal is true to the model: a round gap does not reach a sharp corner. But the user cannot make a finish pass of such a cavity, and the stock sim judges the same burn clean within its tolerance.\n\n**What is wanted:** the size law compares the electrode's outline with the cavity's outline, not their extents. The Sinker Burn then states the cavity's outline (today it states `cavity_x` and `cavity_y` only). A finish is refused only when a wall is left under size by more than the slack.\n\n**Evidence:** `crates/motion/src/sinker_undersize.rs` (the module head and `Undersize::outline`), `crates/app/tests/sinker_electrode_body.rs` (`a_cavity_turned_from_the_axes_is_judged_on_its_outlines_extents`), `docs/decisions/1152-electrode-body.md`.\n\n**Done means:** a finish pass of a diamond pocket with the electrode that `electrode_from_faces` makes for its finish condition is generated, and the program verdict judges it clean. An electrode that is too large for the cavity is still refused by name. The new parameter has its MCP schema entry.\n\nLabels wanted (this account cannot set labels): `enhancement`, `P4`, `effort:high`, `area:3d`, `source:agent`.\n",
